Text2Speech for .NET nanoFramework

This project includes a managed C# port of the PebbleTalk speech synthesizer:
https://github.com/neonfire42/pebbletalk

The port was based on upstream commit:
8ddfbb60b9cd940a8ef4a24c3787ad211b19b003

PebbleTalk copyright (c) 2026 neonfire and is licensed under the MIT License.
The managed port preserves the integer formant synthesis design, English
spelling rules, phoneme data, and waveform lookup data while replacing the C
callback and global state with allocation-bounded .NET nanoFramework classes
and an unsigned 8-bit PCM streaming interface.

The full license for this repository is in LICENSE.

English acoustic calibration attribution

English vowel F1/F2 targets use measurements from:
Hillenbrand, J., Getty, L. A., Clark, M. J., & Wheeler, K. (1995).
"Acoustic characteristics of American English vowels."
The Journal of the Acoustical Society of America, 97(5).
https://doi.org/10.1121/1.411872

The data are hosted with permission from Jim Hillenbrand in:
https://github.com/santiagobarreda/hillenbrand_et_al_1995

The repository wrapper is copyright (c) 2024 Santiago Barreda and is provided
under the MIT License. The original archive has no separate license, and the
original data file states:
Copyright (c) 1995 James Hillenbrand.

The embedded targets conservatively interpolate F1/F2 between the prior
Text2Speech values and adult-male measurement medians. The original
measurements and recordings are not redistributed with this repository.

